lse) set by `cast_spell` for\n  instant/sorcery spells. Restricted mana is spent before unrestricted mana\n  of the same type. Single restriction kind (\"instant/sorcery only\") —\n  deliberate limitation, commented in `engine/mana.py`.\n- **sos_257 animation**: the {5} effect has no \"until end of turn\" in the\n  oracle text, so the animation is permanent — `_original_card_types` is\n  updated so continuous-effect recalculation doesn't strip the creature type.\n  The +1/+0 pump uses a `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` continuous effect (layer 7c).\n\n- **sos_1 engine gaps**: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but never fired —\n  added a fire in `declare_attackers_step` (additive). Replacement effects were\n  only consulted for battlefield-leaving moves; `_resolve_spell` now passes a\n  new `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` and `move_to_zone` also consults\n  replacements for stack-origin moves, so \"exile it instead\" works through the\n  documented seam. Limitation (commented in card): a spell countered via a\n  card-local `_counter_spell` bypasses `move_to_zone` and is not redirected.\n- **sos_1 \"may\" with one candidate**: per TODO, exactly one legal card is\n  auto-selected without a decline prompt; with 2+, `choose_card` returns the\n  card or `None` to decline.\n- **E1 scope**: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired from both `cast_spell` and\n  `cast_spell_free` — casting without paying is still casting (CR 601), and\n  sos_1/sos_120/sos_13 free-cast spells must still trip casualty (sos_226) and\n  the Great Hall pump (sos_257). Copies made by `copy_spell` fire neither\n  (copies are not cast) — matches TODO.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":13,"lines":[" # Key Decisions"," ","+- **sos_120 Paradigm**: per CR 702.192a the recurring \"cast a copy\" only","+  starts the FIRST time a spell with this name resolves — tracked with a","+  per-controller `_paradigm_first_resolved` name set; later real casts are","+  exiled without re-registering. The main-phase copy uses `copy_spell` (no","+  zone residue) rather than creating a card object in exile, per TODO; the","+  copy's own resolution skips the Paradigm clause (it is never in a stack","+  zone). Lands flipped by the exile clause stay exiled without a prompt.","+"," - **sos_57 Wizard check timing**: TODO suggested checking \"you control a","   Wizard\" when the delayed trigger fires; the oracle text leads with the","   condition (\"If you control a Wizard, add … at the beginning of your next"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
