{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cxt3EDiJh4VryhLvSFUQgm","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c64ad6-6cc1-42f5-b9d5-9bf108646c5b","uuid":"abf6e5b6-4c66-431e-9d2b-b8a62fbeba1b","timestamp":"2026-06-11T14:03:08.636Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"# Key Decisions\n","newString":"# Key Decisions\n\n- **sos_97 loyalty targets**: the engine never set `chosen_targets` for\n  loyalty abilities (TODO claimed it did). Added an additive\n  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance.targets` field (default `[]`); `_activate_loyalty_ability`\n  stores them on the StackObject and surfaces them as `source.chosen_targets`\n  at resolution — the same contract spells use. Existing FDN planeswalkers\n  (which read `_resolve_target`) are unaffected.\n- **sos_97 gaps**: `game.rng` (seedable `random.Random`) added to GameState\n  for coin flips; `Player.skip_turns` counter consumed in\n  `GameState.advance_phase`'s turn-wrap logic (a skipped turn passes onward\n  without consuming an extra turn number; composes with the extra-turns\n  queue). Surveil keeps un-binned cards in their existing order (no reorder\n  choice) — commented limitation.\n","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\n- **sos_13 ETB seam**: TODO said register an `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`\n  trigger, but the engine fires that event *before* registering the entering\n  permanent's own triggers (documented convention), so self-ETB triggers are\n  dead code. Mirrored fdn_205: the ETB effect runs in `on_resolve` (counting\n  the still-on-stack card as \"yours\" for the creature comparison). Entry by\n  reanimation therefore skips the ETB — consistent with every FDN ETB card.\n- **sos_13 prepared-copy cost**: CR 722.3c says the controller \"may cast the\n  copy\" (a normal cast) — so the activation pays {W} rather than being free;\n  the copy is then routed through `cast_spell_free` from exile (the engine's\n  cast-from-exile path). Unprepares on cast; a failed cast (no legal target)\n  stays prepared. The resolved copy ends in the graveyard — the engine has no\n  \"copy ceases to exist\" SBA (commented limitation).\n\n- **sos_120 Paradigm**: per CR 702.192a the recurring \"cast a copy\" only\n  starts the FIRST time a spell with this name resolves — tracked with a\n  per-controller `_paradigm_first_resolved` name set; later real casts are\n  exiled without re-registering. The main-phase copy uses `copy_spell` (no\n  zone residue) rather than creating a card object in exile, per TODO; the\n  copy's own resolution skips the Paradigm clause (it is never in a stack\n  zone). Lands flipped by the exile clause stay exiled without a prompt.\n\n- **sos_57 Wizard check timing**: TODO suggested checking \"you control a\n  Wizard\" when the delayed trigger fires; the oracle text leads with the\n  condition (\"If you control a Wizard, add … at the beginning of your next\n  main phase\"), which under standard MTG parsing is evaluated as the spell\n  resolves. Implemented the resolution-time check.\n- **sos_57 \"next main phase\"**: modelled as the next PREcombat main phase —\n  the only main-phase event the engine fires (E2). Commented in the card.\n- **sos_57 mana spent**: `cast_spell` now records\n  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (post-reduction amount actually\n  paid); `cast_spell_free` records 0. Additive engine edit.\n\n- **sos_257 restricted mana**: `ManaPool` grew a parallel `_restricted` store\n  with `add_restricted`/`get_restricted`; `can_pay`/`pay` take a\n  `restricted_ok` keyword (default False) set by `cast_spell` for\n  instant/sorcery spells. Restricted mana is spent before unrestricted mana\n  of the same type. Single restriction kind (\"instant/sorcery only\") —\n  deliberate limitation, commented in `engine/mana.py`.\n- **sos_257 animation**: the {5} effect has no \"until end of turn\" in the\n  oracle text, so the animation is permanent — `_original_card_types` is\n  updated so continuous-effect recalculation doesn't strip the creature type.\n  The +1/+0 pump uses a `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` continuous effect (layer 7c).\n\n- **sos_1 engine gaps**: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but never fired —\n  added a fire in `declare_attackers_step` (additive). Replacement effects were\n  only consulted for battlefield-leaving moves; `_resolve_spell` now passes a\n  new `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` and `move_to_zone` also consults\n  replacements for stack-origin moves, so \"exile it instead\" works through the\n  documented seam. Limitation (commented in card): a spell countered via a\n  card-local `_counter_spell` bypasses `move_to_zone` and is not redirected.\n- **sos_1 \"may\" with one candidate**: per TODO, exactly one legal card is\n  auto-selected without a decline prompt; with 2+, `choose_card` returns the\n  card or `None` to decline.\n- **E1 scope**: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired from both `cast_spell` and\n  `cast_spell_free` — casting without paying is still casting (CR 601), and\n  sos_1/sos_120/sos_13 free-cast spells must still trip casualty (sos_226) and\n  the Great Hall pump (sos_257). Copies made by `copy_spell` fire neither\n  (copies are not cast) — matches TODO.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":18,"lines":[" # Key Decisions"," ","+- **sos_97 loyalty targets**: the engine never set `chosen_targets` for","+  loyalty abilities (TODO claimed it did). Added an additive","+  `LoyaltyAbilityInstance.targets` field (default `[]`); `_activate_loyalty_ability`","+  stores them on the StackObject and surfaces them as `source.chosen_targets`","+  at resolution — the same contract spells use. Existing FDN planeswalkers","+  (which read `_resolve_target`) are unaffected.","+- **sos_97 gaps**: `game.rng` (seedable `random.Random`) added to GameState","+  for coin flips; `Player.skip_turns` counter consumed in","+  `GameState.advance_phase`'s turn-wrap logic (a skipped turn passes onward","+  without consuming an extra turn number; composes with the extra-turns","+  queue). Surveil keeps un-binned cards in their existing order (no reorder","+  choice) — commented limitation.","+"," - **sos_13 ETB seam**: TODO said register an `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`","   trigger, but the engine fires that event *before* registering the entering","   permanent's own triggers (documented convention), so self-ETB triggers are"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
